---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="ART RESIDENCY"
  description="Ndako Home is a seaside residency for creation, reflection, restoration, and intercultural dialogue."
  tone="paper"
>
  <section class="residency-page">
    <h2>NDAKO HOME (LINGALA)</h2>
    <p>
      Installed in a seaside villa, this residency is conceived as a space for
      creation, reflection, and restoration. We invite artists to temporarily
      step away from the pressures of production in order to reconnect with
      their practice, restore mental and physical balance, and develop new
      projects in dialogue with nature.
    </p>
    <p>
      Ndako, in Lingala, means house or home. The choice of naming this
      residency Ndako comes from the desire to make this place somewhere
      creatives and artists truly feel at home, welcomed and embraced.The choice
      of Lingala is deeply connected to the roots of one of the hosts and
      curator Cheria Essieke-Bayer, and stems from a need to create a place
      where memories are shared, good times are lived and new connections are
      made.
    </p>
    <p>
      Located in the village of Gustav Friis, this house has been their
      summerhouse for years, a place full of memories shared with family and
      friends, now opening its doors to creatives and artists. A place where
      peace meets creativity, and where art becomes a medium for reflection,
      connection, renewal and the healing of silent wounds.
    </p>
    <p>
      The residency is both locally rooted and internationally connected. It
      aims to bring together artists from African cultural contexts, artists
      from Denmark, and international artists from diverse backgrounds. The goal
      is to foster meaningful cultural exchange by creating a space for dialogue
      between different artistic practices, life experiences, and worldviews.
    </p>
    <p>
      Artists in residence will be invited to engage with the cultural ecosystem
      of Kolding and its surrounding region, particularly with local artists,
      workshops, and cultural institutions. This includes access to the regional
      contemporary art scene, as well as opportunities for collaboration,
      project presentations, or the initiation of public activities at the local
      and regional levels.
    </p>
    <p>
      As part of the Ubuntu Festival, a cultural festival supported by the
      Municipality of Kolding, artists will also have the opportunity to present
      their work, contribute to a lasting artistic presence, or develop projects
      that directly involve the local community.
    </p>
    <p>
      At the heart of this residency in Bjert is the desire to build lasting
      cultural connections. It is intended as a space conducive to reflection,
      experimentation, and the exploration of themes such as identity,
      environment, movement, and belonging, while strengthening ties between
      local and international creative communities.
    </p>
    <p>
      The residency reflects New Afro's commitment not only to creating
      visibility, but also to building lasting structures that support artistic
      development and intercultural dialogue.
    </p>

    <div class="residency-lists">
      <section>
        <h2>Residents 2026</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Eveline Soum</li>
          <li>Benjamin Abana</li>
          <li>Benga Mavinga</li>
          <li>Jean Baptiste Joire</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>MENTORS</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Chéria Essieke</li>
          <li>Alicia Moon Winding</li>
          <li>Elsy Tobin</li>
          <li>Nuits Balnéaires</li>
          <li>Tobi Onabolu</li>
          <li>Steven Coffi Adjai</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .residency-page {
    font-size: clamp(16px, 1.2vw, 18px);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .residency-page h2 {
    font-family: var(--na-font-headline);
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    font-size: clamp(20px, 2.2vw, 28px);
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .residency-lists {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--na-s-12);
    margin-top: var(--na-s-14);
  }

  .residency-lists ul {
    margin-left: 0;
  }

  .residency-lists li {
    padding-block: 4px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 680px) {
    .residency-lists {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--na-s-8);
    }
  }
</style>
